Hi Ana,
Yes, I have often sent MatchIt my own propensity score, using the code Kosuke is referring you to below.

As for the Mahalanobis distance, you can either match on the Mahalanobis distance of all of the variables you list in the propensity score formula (so then it isn't really a propensity score; the formula is just the way of sending the variable names) by just saying distance="mahalanobis"  ( http://gking.harvard.edu/node/4355/rbuild_documentation/Additional_Arguments_f.html).

If you want to do a Mahalanobis match on a few variables within propensity score calipers you can also do that, by specifying your normal propensity score model in the formula and then adding the mahvars=c("x1", "x2") option ( http://gking.harvard.edu/node/4355/rbuild_documentation/Additional_Arguments_f3.html).

Thanks,
Liz


